      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the person in the image",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the person (wearing a kippah in front of the American flag), as the meme uses this individual as a symbolic representation of 'jews and americans' according to the hateful stereotype. The absence of explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me' means the projection is implicit through the visual and textual framing, where the viewer is expected to identify with or interpret the scene as representing themselves or their group in relation to the stereotype.",
